{{also|Tinker}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/tɪŋkə(ɹ)/}}, {{X-SAMPA|/tINk@(r)/}}
* {{rhymes|ɪŋkə(r)}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|tinkere|lang=enm}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# an [[itinerant]] tinsmith and [[mender]] of [[household]] [[utensil]]s made of tin
# {{context|dated|chiefly|British|and|Irish|offensive|lang=en}} A member of the [[travelling]] community. A [[gypsy]].
# {{context|usually with "little"|lang=en}} A [[mischievous]] person, especially a playful, [[impish]] youngster.
# Someone who repairs, or attempts repair on anything mechanical (tinkers) or invents.
# The act of repair or invention.
# {{context|military|obsolete|lang=en}} A small [[mortar]] on the end of a [[staff]].
# Any of various fish: the [[chub]] [[mackerel]], the [[silverside]], the [[skate]], or a young mackerel about two years old.
# A bird, the razor-billed [[auk]].

{{Webster 1913}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|mischievous person}} [[rapscallion]], [[rascal]], [[rogue]], [[scamp]], [[scoundrel]]
* {{sense|member of the travelling community}} [[traveller]]

